```# ArrayList

[![ArrayList CI](https://github.com/adamkrivka/ArrayList/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/adamkrivka/ArrayList/actions/workflows/ci.yml)

ArrayList is a C# class library for manipulating dynamic arrays. It works with any .NET language that can use C#, including C# itself. In C#, an ArrayList can be used wherever you can use an array.

This implementation is efficient and provides methods for adding, removing, and accessing elements. It also supports methods to sort, search, and resize the list. The class is designed to operate efficiently on arrays, which is the primary function of ArrayList. It can handle adding and removal of elements at either the end or beginning of the list, and it preserves the order of items.

The most significant feature of an ArrayList is that it will automatically resize to accommodate any number of elements. This ensures that you don't need to worry about the size of the array when you add or remove items. 

Please keep in mind this is my implementation of ArrayLists for learning purposes and it's not partnered with Microsoft, and thus it may not have the same level of robustness and features as those implemented by Microsoft in their .NET framework libraries.

# Features

- Dynamic array: Built on an underlying dynamic array, the size of which increases or decreases automatically.
- Efficient for adding, removing and accessing elements.
- Efficiently handles adding and removing elements at both the beginning and end of the list.
- Preserves the order of items.
- Sorted Lists: Supports sorting, searching and provides methods to access elements in a sorted list.
- Supports resizing.

# Usage

```csharp
using System;
using ArrayList;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        ArrayList arrayList = new ArrayList();

        arrayList.Add(1);
        arrayList.Add(2);
        arrayList.Add(3);

        Console.WriteLine(arrayList.ToString());
    }
}
```

